<task id="080" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Restore cross-record search by authorizing the PAGE of results — scope=all stops being refused and starts being filtered</title>
    <phase>0c Secure Documents — Wave 1 (added mid-wave)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Re-opens a scope that was a live tenant-wide disclosure eight days ago. The filtering IS the security boundary; a bug here restores the original hole.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The failure mode is a plausible-looking wrong answer — a partially-filtered result set looks exactly like a correctly-filtered one. That needs judgement, not throughput.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Must be correct under adversarial reading, and must also fix a second pre-existing defect (the code page never sends entityId) to be usable.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>wave1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies the same filter and endpoint as task 070, and shares the surface with 077.</parallel-reason>
